[2026.09.08-05.34.46:173][ 92]LogVoxelSky: VoxelSky SkyLight capture point now z=0.0 m (voxel.Sky.SkyLightAtGroundZ=0; the spawn column's ground is 1644.2 m, sea level is 0.0 m). THIS IS WHERE THE REAL-TIME CAPTURE IS RENDERED FROM (USkyLightComponent::SendRenderTransform_Concurrent -> FSkyLightSceneProxy::CapturePosition -> the cube view's ViewOrigin), so it is where the ambient term that lights every surface in this world is integrated -- and at night, with the moon down, it is the ONLY thing lighting them. At 0 the capture also sits far below the height fog's reference height, so it integrates fog rather than sky; voxel.Sky.FogInSkyCapture 0 is the other arm of that pair, and the fog's own APPLIED line prints the density at both altitudes.
