[2026.09.08-05.34.46:181][ 92]LogVoxelEarth: VoxelSky dome SHOWN (voxel.Sky.DomeEnabled=1, voxel.Sky.Enabled=1). This is the mesh only -- the light rig, the atmosphere and the exposure curve are unaffected either way, which is what makes DomeEnabled a clean A/B for 'how much of the night frame is the star dome'.
[2026.09.08-05.34.46:181][ 92]LogVoxelEarth: VoxelSky ATMOSPHERE DOME SHOWN (voxel.Sky.AtmosphereDome=1, materialValid=1 -> resolved 1). SHOWN means THIS MESH paints the sky and the SkyAtmosphere's full-screen pass does not (View.bSceneHasSkyMaterial goes true, SkyAtmosphereRendering.cpp:2214); HIDDEN hands the sky back to that pass. The two must agree to within 2/255 of mean luma at every hour -- that is the whole of phase S1, and this line is what tells a capture which arm it is.
